th/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math>&nbsp;candies, is equal to"}, "options": [{"id": "e99a33", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>205</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925fe08"}, {"id": "370977", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>615</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925fe09"}, {"id": "f4975b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>510</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925fe0a"}, {"id": "9c447a", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>430</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925fe0b"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925fe0c", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfa3"], "topics": ["60c9e88bea076dc381c0e100"], "concepts": ["6162fc2a6ed13040ec8576cb"], "question": {"text": "Let<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>2</mn></math> be an integer. Suppose that there are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math> Metro stations in a city located around a circular path. Each pair of the nearest stations is connected by a straight track only. Further, each pair of the nearest station&nbsp;is connected by blue line, whereas all remaining pairs of stations are connected by red line. If number&nbsp;of red lines is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>99</mn></math> times the number of blue lines, then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math> is"}, "options": [{"id": "2bfc4d", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>201</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925fe0d"}, {"id": "901fc2", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>200</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f462ee0e063d925fe0e"}, {"id": "961dbe", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://